    <text>
        <body>
            <div xml:id="d781">

                <pb facs="0792" n="680" sameAs="frus:frus1919Russia/pg680"/>

                <note rend="inline" type="source">Paris Peace Conference 184.01502/39:
                    Telegram</note>
                <head><hi rendition="#italic">The Commission to Negotiate
                            Peace to the Chargé in Denmark</hi> (<hi
                            rendition="#italic">Grant-Smith</hi>)</head>
                <opener><dateline rendition="#float-right"><placeName><hi rendition="#small-caps"
                                >Paris</hi></placeName>, <date calendar="gregorian"
                            when="1919-06-10T23:00:00+01:00"><hi rendition="#italic">June 10, 1919,
                                11 p.m.</hi></date></dateline></opener>
                <p>65. For Greene, Libau.</p>
                <p>Your 399, 2d, referring to increase of Russian volunteer force. Your telegram has
                    been referred to General Harries<anchor n="20"
                        xml:id="d781-f1"/> now in Paris who believes that Prince
                        Lieven should be allowed all the volunteers <pb
                        facs="0793" n="681" xml:id="pg681"/> he wants and sees no reason why the
                    number of prisoners available for him should be limited except that policy has
                    been adopted to send a small number of troops from various camps each day in
                    order not to show partiality and on account of difficulties of transportation.
                    General Harries has been requested by Am[erican] mission to
                    act according to his discretion in the matter and the only suggestion made to
                    him is that the prisoners going with Lieven’s force shall
                    be genuine volunteers for that service and shall not use their enlistment as a
                    mere pretext to obtain an early release.</p>
                <closer><hi rendition="#small-caps">Am</hi>[<hi rendition="#small-caps">erican</hi>]
                        <hi rendition="#small-caps">Mission</hi></closer>
            </div>
        </body>
    </text>
    <standOff>
        <listAnnotation>
            <note corresp="#d781-f1" n="20" xml:id="d781-f1-content">
                <p>Brig. Gen. George H. Harries, chief of the American Military
                    Mission at Berlin.</p>
            </note>
